Description: ASoC: soc-pcm: apply symmetry only against another stream
 A link with symmetric rates or sample bits rejects a stream's
 hw_params that differ from its CPU DAI's, but once the stream has had
 hw_params those are its own, and they stay until hw_free: a second
 hw_params with other values was rejected against itself. OSS
 emulation makes one as each setting changes, the first with its
 defaults (8 kHz), so on the Chumby Classic's TSC2100, whose codec asks
 for both symmetries, /dev/dsp refused any rate or format but those.
 (5.9 checked the CPU DAIs' own symmetry alone, which the i.MX SSI
 doesn't ask for.) A DAI that another stream has active is still held
 to its parameters.
Author: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AI generated code]
Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/soc-pcm.c b/sound/soc/soc-pcm.c
index 3137c09..eec6cbb 100644
--- a/sound/soc/soc-pcm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-pcm.c
@@ -599,6 +599,7 @@ static int soc_pcm_params_symmetry(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	if (symmetry)							\
 		for_each_rtd_cpu_dais(rtd, i, cpu_dai)			\
 			if (!snd_soc_dai_is_dummy(cpu_dai) &&		\
+			    snd_soc_dai_active(cpu_dai) > 1 &&		\
 			    cpu_dai->symmetric_##xxx &&			\
 			    cpu_dai->symmetric_##xxx != d.symmetric_##xxx) \
 				return snd_soc_ret(rtd->dev, -EINVAL,	\
@@ -606,7 +607,13 @@ static int soc_pcm_params_symmetry(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 						   #xxx, cpu_dai->name, cpu_dai->symmetric_##xxx, \
 						   d.name, d.symmetric_##xxx);

-	/* reject unmatched parameters when applying symmetry */
+	/*
+	 * Reject unmatched parameters when applying symmetry, against a DAI
+	 * that another stream has active too. One this stream alone has
+	 * active holds only this stream's earlier parameters, which a
+	 * second hw_params may change (OSS emulation makes one as each
+	 * setting changes).
+	 */
 	__soc_pcm_params_symmetry(rate);
 	__soc_pcm_params_symmetry(channels);
 	__soc_pcm_params_symmetry(sample_bits);
